{
  "reasons": {
    "no-greek-verse-43": "Swete's Greek has no verse here: LXX2012's Psalm 43:8 ('For you have saved us from them that afflicted us, and have put to shame them that hated us.') is Brenton's, from the Hebrew, and the Greek verse 43:8 is empty, so there is no Greek word to point at (mw-u2w5klk.349.13).",
    "next-verse-33-43": "LXX2012 carries English of the next Greek verse here (Psalm 33:17's 'The righteous cried, and the Lord listened to them,' is Swete's 33:18, and Psalm 43:21's 'search these things out?' is Swete's 43:22 'οὐχὶ ὁ θεὸς ἐκζητήσει ταῦτα'): the Greek words are in the other verse, which has no chunk of its own to hold them (mw-u2w5klk.349.13).",
    "paired-or-added-psa": "Either the Greek word that renders it is a pair the aligner made to another English word that the pass does not touch (a 'the' or a verb crossed with its neighbour, as 'afflict' of 3:2 sits beside θλίβοντες on 'many'), or Brenton adds it to make English of a Greek phrase ('O Lord', 'the one that', 'saying', 'whole burnt'); each was read against its verse and no free Greek word of its verse renders it (mw-u2w5klk.349.13)."
  },
